      "ground": "The argument mischaracterizes the legal standard by conflating the absolute prohibition in Article 16 with the 'military objective' exception in Article 52.",
      "reasoning": "Article 16 of Additional Protocol II prohibits acts of hostility against historic monuments unless they are used in support of the military effort. It does not contain the 'imperatively demanded by military necessity' standard cited in the argument, which belongs to Article 52. The Trial Chamber found the bridge was used for combat activities, potentially negating its protected status under Article 16, making the 'military necessity' justification irrelevant to the specific prohibition invoked.",
