          "article": "16"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "target_argument_id": "arg_733f60b5",
      "ground": "The argument incorrectly applies the 'wanton' requirement by treating a military motive as equivalent to the specific intent required by the statute.",
      "reasoning": "Article 8(2)(a)(iv) requires destruction to be 'carried out wantonly,' a standard distinct from mere intent or military motive. While the Chamber found a motive to sap morale, establishing 'wantonness' requires proof that the destruction was carried out without any military necessity or justification, not merely that the motive was secondary. The argument fails to distinguish between 'unlawful' and 'wanton' as separate legal elements, conflating the two to satisfy the statutory test.",
      "severity": "material",
