      "target_argument_id": "arg_1fb6506f",
      "ground": "The argument relies on a misquoted provision, attributing the 'devastation' language to Article 8(2)(a)(iv) when the statute addresses 'extensive destruction' of property.",
      "reasoning": "The Rome Statute does not use the term 'devastation of a town' in Article 8(2)(a)(iv); it criminalizes 'extensive destruction and appropriation of property.' While the underlying conduct may be similar, the legal characterization must align with the precise statutory language. The argument’s reliance on 'devastation' as a distinct legal element not found in the cited provision weakens its doctrinal foundation, as it fails to map the facts onto the correct statutory text.",
